  "worked_solution": "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(B),$ then the equation $Bx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[B\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 7 & k-3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 7 & k-3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k+2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 0=k-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-1,$ which means that $k=1.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
